===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*speh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|spede||prosperity, good luck, quickness, success}}, from {{inh|en|ang|spēd||success}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*spōdi||prosperity, success}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*spōan}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*spōaną||to prosper, succeed, be happy}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*speh₁-||to prosper, turn out well}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|spede}}, {{m|sco|speid||success, quickness, speed}}, {{cog|nl|spoed||haste; speed}}, {{cog|nds-de|Spood||haste; speed; eagerness; success}}, {{cog|de|Sput||progress, acceleration, haste}}. Related also to {{cog|ang|spōwan||to be successful, succeed}}, {{cog|sq|shpejt||to speed, to hurry}} and {{cog|ru|спеши́ть||to hurry}}, {{cog|la|spēs||hope, expectation}}, {{m|la|spērō||hope|pos=verb}}, perhaps also to {{cog|grc|σπεύδω||to urge on, hasten, press on}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# The state of moving quickly or the capacity for rapid motion.
#: {{syn|en|celerity|rapidity|velocity|Thesaurus:speed}}
#: {{ux|en|How does Usain Bolt run at that '''speed'''?}}
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=i|page=17|passage=Returne with '''ſpeed''', time paſſeth ſwift away,<br>Our life is fraile, and we may dye to day.}}
